    "body": "Hmm, I'm still kind of confused. I think that section of the spec is just saying that keygen serializes as a void element, right? And I don't believe I removed that in this diff. I also don't understand what that would have to do with the innerText/outerText setters, which should be related to parsing, not serialization...\r\n\r\nIn any case, that ieForbidsInsertHTML function is fascinating... probably it should just be removed, as Edge at least doesn't seem to follow it anymore.",
